      "extract": "msp ALGEBRA AND NUMBER THEORY 14:7 (2020) https://doi.org/10.2140/ant.2020.14.1911 Burgess bounds for short character sums evaluated at forms Lillian B. Pierce and Junyan Xu We establish a Burgess bound for short multiplicative character sums in arbitrary dimensions, in which the character is evaluated at a homogeneous form that belongs to a very general class of “admissible” forms. This n-dimensional Burgess bound",
