      "extract": "The celebrated Burgess bound [1957] proves that for χ a nonprincipal multiplicative Dirichlet character modulo a prime q, the character sum S(N, H) = X x∈Z N<x≤N+H χ(x) is bounded for every integer r ≥1 by |S(N, H)| ≪r H1−1/rq(r+1)/4r2 log q. (1-1) From this it can be deduced that S(N, H) admits a nontrivial bound o(H) for H as small as H = q1/4+κ, for any κ > 0. Bounds for S(N, H) have many applications, and as we",
